  "id": "COMPOUND:43665 - PROTEIN:5814",
  "verbalization": "Lippiolidolic acid appears to have a shared target of SNU-387, which is involved in multiple pathways leading to VMRC-MELG. The evidence suggests that Lippiolidolic acid may act as a modulator of SNU-387, which in turn influences VMRC-MELG through various biochemical mechanisms. The presence of multiple targets of SNU-387, including compounds like 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One and 5-Hydroxytryptophan monohydrate, dl-, indicates a complex network of interactions. These findings suggest that Lippiolidolic acid may exert its effects through a mechanism that involves SNU-387, potentially by modulating its downstream targets, which ultimately lead to VMRC-MELG. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of SNU-387 in mediating the relationship between Lippiolidolic acid and VMRC-MELG, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
